    "body": "## Overview\r\n\r\n`tokenspeed-mla` depends on `tokenspeed-triton` which uses nanobind. Upstream Triton also switched to nanobind in 3.9 (triton-lang/triton#10283). Older `tokenspeed-triton` builds register the same C++ types in nanobind's shared registry, so loading both aborts with `Critical nanobind error: refusing to add duplicate key \"PAD_ZERO\"`. This breaks vLLM CI on the torch 2.15 RC and nightly lanes (pytorch/test-infra#9050).\r\n\r\n[`tokenspeed-triton` 3.9.10.post20261008](https://github.com/lightseekorg/triton/tree/release/3.9.10.post20261008) uses its own nanobind domain, so the copies no longer collide, and `tokenspeed-mla` requires it from 0.2.20. This PR bumps the `tokenspeed-mla` pin from 0.2.15 to 0.2.21 to pick up that fix.\r\n\r\n## Claims\r\n\r\n- Fixes the `PAD_ZERO` abort with Triton 3.9.\r\n- No numerical change on the TokenSpeed MLA path.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\nAll tested on B200\r\n\r\n**Fixes the pytorch/test-infra#9050 repro** (torch 2.15.0 + triton 3.9.0):\r\n\r\n| Check | 0.2.15 (tokenspeed-triton 3.8.10) | 0.2.21 (tokenspeed-triton 3.9.10) |\r\n| --- | --- | --- |\r\n| `import triton; import tokenspeed_triton`, both orders, Python 3.11/3.12 | abort | pass |\r\n| `test_supported_backend_preserves_dcp_eligibility[TOKENSPEED_MLA]` | abort | 1 passed |\r\n| `test_attention_selector.py` | - | 97 passed, 14 skipped |\r\n| `test_mla_backends.py -k tokenspeed_mla` | - | 307 passed, 290 skipped |\r\n| Both Tritons' kernels + `torch.compile` in one process | - | pass |\r\n\r\n**No behavior change** (torch 2.13, same compiler):\r\n\r\n| Check | 0.2.15 | 0.2.21 |\r\n| --- | --- | --- |\r\n| `test_mla_backends.py -k tokenspeed_mla` | 307 passed, 290 skipped | 307 passed, 290 skipped |\r\n| TokenSpeed decode tests (accuracy, CUDA graphs, split-KV) | - | 191 passed, 53 skipped (SM107) |\r\n| Decode/prefill outputs with vLLM's arguments, 14 cases | baseline | bitwise identical |\r\n| GSM8K, eager x2 | 0.7832, 0.7771 | 0.7786, 0.7771 |\r\n| GSM8K, CUDA graphs x2 | 0.7839, 0.7665 | 0.7718, 0.7763 |\r\n\r\n**Installs correctly:** `uv pip compile` picks `tokenspeed-triton==3.9.10.post20261008` on the default and nightly indexes. `pre-commit` passes; `requirements/test/cuda.txt` is unchanged.\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Commands</summary>\r\n\r\nB200 (sm100), driver 580.82.07, CUDA 13.0, Python 3.12. torch 2.15 env: torch 2.15.0+cu130 and triton 3.9.0 from `https://download.pytorch.org/whl/test/cu130`; vLLM via `tools/use_existing_torch.py` and `VLLM_USE_PRECOMPILED=1`.\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npython -c \"import triton; import tokenspeed_triton\"\r\npython -c \"import tokenspeed_triton; import triton\"\r\npytest -v \"tests/kernels/attention/test_attention_selector.py::test_supported_backend_preserves_dcp_eligibility[TOKENSPEED_MLA]\"\r\npytest -v tests/kernels/attention/test_attention_selector.py\r\npytest -v tests/v1/attention/test_mla_backends.py -k tokenspeed_mla\r\npytest -s tests/evals/gsm8k/test_gsm8k_correctness.py --config-list-file=<list>\r\n# lightseekorg/tokenspeed at the release commit:\r\npytest -v tokenspeed-mla/tests/test_mla_decode.py\r\n```\r\n\r\nGSM8K server args: `--max-model-len 4096 --attention-backend TOKENSPEED_MLA --kv-cache-dtype fp8_e4m3 --block-size 64`, plus `--enforce-eager` for the eager runs.\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n\r\n- Mechanism: neither upstream Triton nor older `tokenspeed-triton` sets `NB_DOMAIN`. The fixed `tokenspeed-triton` sets `NB_DOMAIN=tokenspeed`, and `tokenspeed-mla` 0.2.20+ requires it (lightseekorg/tokenspeed#2134).\r\n- The 0.2.15 pin still allows the old `tokenspeed-triton`; the bump makes the fixed version required.\r\n- Also picks up lightseekorg/tokenspeed#2132, which fixes an illegal memory access in decode when `tokenspeed_mla_min_split_kv` > 1 produces 256 MiB or more of partials.\r\n- Authored with assistance from Claude.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\r\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\r\n\r\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\r\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\r\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\r\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n\r\n",
